S7 generics giving \code{SummarizedExperiment}-style access to the three
levels of an \link{IsoformicExperiment}. All of them return in-memory tibbles
or matrices; the annotation tables are read from Parquet on first use
and cached (see the class documentation).

\strong{Samples}
\itemize{
\item \code{col_data()}, \verb{col_data<-}: sample metadata (\code{sample_id} first).
\item \code{col_names()}: sample IDs of the assays.
}

\strong{Transcript level}
\itemize{
\item \code{assays()}, \code{assay(x, name)}, \code{assay_names()}, \verb{assay<-}: transcript
matrices. \code{assay()} without a name returns the first assay.
\item \code{row_names()}: transcript IDs of the assays.
\item \code{row_data()}: transcript annotation (with gene columns) for the assayed
transcripts, in assay row order.
\item \code{tx_annot()}: the same join for \emph{all} annotated transcripts.
\item \code{tx_to_gene()}: two-column transcript/gene mapping.
}

\strong{Gene level}
\itemize{
\item \code{gene_assays()}, \code{gene_assay(x, name)}, \verb{gene_assays<-}: gene matrices,
derived by summing isoforms unless set explicitly.
\item \code{gene_data()}: gene annotation for the genes represented in the assays.
\item \code{gene_names()}: gene IDs of the gene assays.
}

